      "writtenOn": "2022-09-16T13:17:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "by default, modules in `Blueprint` in tests are in the always convert list, so `bazel_module: { bp2build_available: true },` is redundant.\n\nI was asking if we should instead set `bazel_module: { bp2build_available: false },` in `barlib`. While it is true that we would need the stubs to be migrated in the actual migration, during testing, we often set `bazel_module: { bp2build_available: false },` for the modules that are not the focus of the test to keep the test focused on the details we care about.",
      "parentUuid": "1e9f8725_d65687ec",
